# Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) Device Tokens
#
# Add one device token per line
# Lines starting with # are ignored
#
# To get a device token:
# 1. Implement FCM in your mobile app
# 2. Call the appropriate method to retrieve the token:
#    - iOS: Messaging.messaging().token
#    - Android: FirebaseMessaging.getInstance().token
#    - Web: getToken(messaging)
#
# Example tokens (replace with your actual tokens):
example-device-token-1:APA91bEXAMPLE_TOKEN_REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_TOKEN_FROM_YOUR_APP
example-device-token-2:APA91bANOTHER_EXAMPLE_TOKEN_REPLACE_WITH_REAL_TOKEN
# example-device-token-3:APA91bCOMMENTED_OUT_TOKEN_EXAMPLE

# Note: Real FCM tokens are typically 150+ characters long and contain
# a mix of letters, numbers, underscores, and hyphens